<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/04TS">Exercise <span data-tag="04TS">10.2.0.5</span>.</a> Let $f: R \rightarrow S$ be a homomorphism of commutative rings. Show that $f$ is a regular epimorphism (in the category of commutative rings) if and only if it is surjective (as a map of sets). In particular, the inclusion map $\mathbf{Z} \hookrightarrow \mathbf{Q}$ of Example <a data-tag="04TN" href="/tag/04TN">10.2.0.1</a> is an epimorphism in the category of commutative rings which is not regular. </p>
